<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Purang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Burang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Purang, or Burang, is a district in the far west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> Autonomous Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, near the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, close to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-manasarovar">Lake Manasarovar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-kailash">Mount Kailash</a>. In the 10th and 11th centuries it formed with Guge the kingdom founded by the descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyide-nyimagon">Kyide Nyimagon</a>, and later the Khasa Mallas of western Nepal held it. Its main town, Taklakot, has long been a trading post on routes to Nepal and India.</p></div>
